{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1569247405,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzNDExMzY3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3698#issuecomment-534113672"},"message":"The problem (worked around with de4d7545b in gh-3648) is that the example creates a toy output file by running `file` on locked git-annex files, and (I think) git-annex confuses that file for an unlocked pointer file because there is an annex object path in the first line.\n\n```\n$ echo one \u003eone\n$ echo two \u003etwo\n$ git annex add one two \n$ git commit -mc1\n$ file one two \u003eres    \n\n$ git annex add res \nadd res ok\n(recording state in git...)\ngit-annex: git status will show res to be modified, since content availability has changed and git-annex was unable to update the index. This is only a cosmetic problem affecting git status; git add, git commit, etc won't be affected. To fix the git status display, you can run: git update-index -q --refresh res\n\n$ git diff\ndiff --git a/res b/res\nindex 0b93d4a..f3ce9f7 100644\n--- a/res\n+++ b/res\n@@ -1,2 +1 @@\n-one: symbolic link to .git/annex/objects/0J/J1/SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806/SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\n-two: symbolic link to .git/annex/objects/xM/1g/SHA256E-s4--27dd8ed44a83ff94d557f9fd0412ed5a8cbca69ea04922d88c01184a07300a5a/SHA256E-s4--27dd8ed44a83ff94d557f9fd0412ed5a8cbca69ea04922d88c01184a07300a5a\n+/annex/objects/SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\n\n$ git commit -am\"c2\"\n$ git cat-file -p HEAD:res\n/annex/objects/SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1569255640,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI2NTUwNzk0ODA="},"added":["fix-implem